     rrddsseettrroooott — insert disk image into RAMDISK kernel

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     rrddsseettrroooott --ss _k_e_r_n_e_l
     rrddsseettrroooott [--ddxx] _k_e_r_n_e_l [_d_i_s_k_._f_s]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rrddsseettrroooott utility inserts the file _d_i_s_k_._f_s into the reserved space
     inside a RAMDISK kernel.  If _d_i_s_k_._f_s is not specified, rrddsseettrroooott reads
     from standard input.

     The options are as follows:

     --dd      Debug.

     --ss      Print the size in bytes of the reserved space in the RAMDISK ker‐
             nel.  No insertion or extraction is attempted.

     --xx      Rather than inserting, extract the _d_i_s_k_._f_s image.  If _d_i_s_k_._f_s is
             not specified, rrddsseettrroooott writes to standard output.  The disk can
             be made accessible using vnconfig(8), filesystems can be manipu‐
             lated, and finally re-inserted into the RAMDISK kernel.

